# compactc 0.34.0's generated `initialState` for
# `wrapped_points.compact` beside this file (4 fields, each a Cell of a record
# holding a curve point: the atom sequences of minocrab's generic `evm_flow`
# wrappers `Owned`, `Outstanding`, `HandleOwned` and `QueueEntry` with a point
# for their type parameter; no constructor, no circuits),
# run in node 22 on compact-runtime 0.19.0 + @midnightntwrk/onchain-runtime-v4 4.0.0-rc.3
# (= ledger-9.1.0.0-rc.3, the runtime compactc 0.34.0 targets; `checkRuntimeVersion('0.19.0')`
# passes). Produced by project 00002's JS oracle in P6's fix pass on 2026-09-23 (audit R2)
# (experiments/00002-tools/js-oracle/initial-state.mjs via run-initial.sh: node:22-bookworm-slim,
# --network none, two runs byte-identical); compactc from the pinned release archive (Docker
# image aa-compactc:0.34.0, `--skip-zk --feature-zkir-v3`, two compiles byte-identical).
#
# The bytes: `ContractState.serialize()` of a DEFAULT ContractState whose `data` is the initial
# state's `data` (no operations, default maintenance authority, empty balance) — the tagged
# `midnight:contract-state[v8]` form of the state tree alone. `tests/ledger_deploy.rs` compares
# it with `ContractState::new(initial_state().build(), {}, Default::default())`, serialized.
#
# Shape: Array(4) of Cells. compactc's JS defaults a record member by member, so each point
# inside a record is at its Compact identity (Secp256k1Point `(p-1, p-1, 1)`, JubjubPoint
# `(0, 1)`) and every other member is empty.
